Root cause:
The bug was caused by an assumption that tunnels which can be offloaded (determined by `mlxsw_sp_ipip_ops.can_offload()`) would always have a corresponding IPIP entry. However, if a tunnel was demoted to slow path due to a conflict with its local address, it would not have a valid IPIP entry, leading to a failure in the initialization function `mlxsw_sp_nexthop_ipip_init()`. This failure triggered a FIB (Forwarding Information Base) abort in the system, which needed to be resolved by checking for the existence of an IPIP entry before proceeding with further tunnel operations.
